# Rust
/target
**/*.rs.bk
# Cargo.lock IS committed: this workspace produces a distributable wheel, so we
# pin the exact arrow/datafusion/pyo3 resolution for reproducible builds.

# Python / maturin
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
/dist
/wheelhouse
*.so
*.pyd
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# JavaScript: one bun workspace rooted here, with `viz/` (the shared visual
# layer) and `site/` (the Astro docs site) as members. The single /bun.lock IS
# committed so the deploy build is reproducible and `bun install
# --frozen-lockfile` has something to check against.
#
# node_modules is unanchored: bun hoists to the workspace root but still places
# per-member directories, so an anchored /site/node_modules/ rule would leave the
# root and viz/ copies untracked-but-visible.
node_modules/
/site/dist/
/site/.astro/
/site/.wrangler/

# Credentials. Wrangler reads `.env` from the project directory, so a Cloudflare
# API token can land here by accident — never commit one.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.dev.vars

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
